            <ArticleTitle>Coronary air embolism during coronary angioplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>164-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case is described in which the use of the Hartzler microcatheter during coronary angioplasty resulted in coronary air embolism. The recognition, prevention, and mechanism of this occurrence are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
